# Development — leave API/WS bases empty so the browser uses same-origin `/api` and `/ws`
# (Vite proxies below). Production builds inject absolute bases via Docker / nginx.
# Dev server ignores absolute VITE_* bases unless you set (rare: remote API from dev UI):
# VITE_DEV_ABSOLUTE_API=true
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_WS_BASE_URL=
VITE_APP_ENV=development

# TradingView embed: set "true" for production static builds. Omitted in prod = off; dev server defaults on unless "false".
VITE_FEATURE_TRADINGVIEW=

# Production — set these in compose / runtime env when baking the static bundle:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://polaris.internal
# VITE_WS_BASE_URL=wss://polaris.internal

# Never put POLARIS_PANIC_KEY here for production builds — use dev-only `.env.local` if needed.
# VITE_POLARIS_PANIC_KEY=

# Vite dev server process only (not exposed to the browser). Proxy targets for `/api` + `/ws`.
# Default 127.0.0.1 avoids some `localhost` → IPv6 (::1) mismatches when the API binds IPv4-only.
# ATLAS_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ATLAS_API_PORT=8787
#
# Enables the dashboard “Start everything + open dashboard” button (POST /__atlas_dev__/launch-full-stack).
# Never enable on untrusted networks. Example: ATLAS_VITE_LAUNCH_STACK=1 npm run dev
# ATLAS_VITE_LAUNCH_STACK=
